# Environment this IMAGE fixes. See Dockerfile.capability (`<profile>.env`).
#
# FlashInfer is the one attention backend this image cannot use: its kernels are
# compiled on first use and no image here ships a CUDA toolkit, so an engine that
# selects it dies during init with
#   flashinfer/jit/cpp_ext.py: Could not find nvcc and default
#   cuda_home='/usr/local/cuda' doesn't exist
# (measured on a pod 2026-10-22, on the fleet image, when an FP8 KV cache was
# asked for). The fleet image now carries flashinfer-jit-cache so it CAN; this
# one deliberately does not, because the OCR models never ask for that dtype and
# the package costs ~2.9 GiB.
#
# Which backend vLLM picks for a given card is a property of the vLLM VERSION,
# not of anything configured here -- so the next vLLM bump could start preferring
# FlashInfer on Ampere and this image would stop booting, for a reason nothing in
# its own configuration would explain. Pinning it means a bump can change
# throughput, never whether the pod starts.
#
# FLASH_ATTN is vLLM's own default on Ampere for these models; it is named rather
# than inherited.
VLLM_ATTENTION_BACKEND=FLASH_ATTN
